# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA — never commit.
# The ITSM exports contain employee names, employee IDs, email addresses and
# full ticket bodies. None of it belongs in version control.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
*.tsv
*.pdf
*.docx
data/
exports/
uploads/

# A pg_dump of the database is EVERYTHING - every employee name, every
# employee ID, every ticket body, every password hash - in one file. The
# default BACKUP_DIR is backups/ inside this folder, which is convenient on
# day one and is why these three lines exist. Set BACKUP_DIR in api/.env to
# somewhere outside the repository and off this machine; api/backup.js warns
# on every run until you do.
backups/
*.dump
*.backup

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS — never commit.
# .clasp.json holds the Apps Script project ID that links this folder to your
# Google account. Keep it local; .clasp.json.example shows the shape.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.clasp.json
.clasprc.json
*.env
credentials.json

# api/.env holds the PostgreSQL password. *.env above does match a bare
# .env - git's glob allows the * to match nothing - but this is a database
# password in a public repository, so it is spelled out rather than left to
# a reader working out glob semantics. api/.env.example is the safe copy.
.env
api/.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# clasp writes server files as .js unless .clasp.json says fileExtension: gs.
# This repository names them .gs, so a .js in here is a SECOND copy of a file
# that is already tracked - and the next `clasp push` would upload both and
# give the Apps Script project two of every function. Ignored so one cannot be
# committed by accident; .clasp.json.example says why it should not exist at
# all.
src/*.js

# The harness page is assembled from src/ by tests/harness/build.js. It is a
# build artifact - half a megabyte that changes on every edit to any source
# file - so it is rebuilt rather than committed.
tests/harness/page.html

# Screenshots rendered from the harness to show a change before it is pasted
# into Apps Script. Same reasoning as the page above: generated, and stale the
# moment anything is edited.
preview/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
